// oleg.ae/for-laura: explains to Laura Moiseja (Boldane client) why her 2026-10-14 interviews produced 29 posts.
// Unlisted, noindex. Generated by a one-off script in a Boldane admin session (2026-10-20).
export const HTML = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\"><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\"><title>Why you got 29 posts</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"What happened after your interviews on 14 October.\">\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#f6f7f9;--card:#fff;--ink:#14181f;--mut:#5d6573;--line:#e3e6eb;--blue:#2863f0;--green:#15803d;--green-bg:#e8f6ed;--amber:#b45309;--amber-bg:#fdf3e4}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{--bg:#0b0f16;--card:#121823;--ink:#e6e9ee;--mut:#9aa3b2;--line:#242c3a;--blue:#6b93ff;--green:#5bd28a;--green-bg:#122619;--amber:#f0a654;--amber-bg:#2a1f12}}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html{-webkit-text-size-adjust:100%}\nbody{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",Inter,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;padding:32px 16px 56px}\nh1{font-size:28px;line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 14px}h2{font-size:20px;margin:36px 0 10px}\np{margin:0 0 12px}.mut{color:var(--mut)}\n.badge{display:inline-block;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;border-radius:999px;padding:3px 10px;margin-bottom:10px}\n.box{border-radius:14px;padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--card)}\n.new{border-color:var(--green)}.new .badge{background:var(--green-bg);color:var(--green)}\n.old{border-color:var(--amber)}.old .badge{background:var(--amber-bg);color:var(--amber)}\n.post p{font-size:16px;margin:0 0 10px}\n.old ul{margin:4px 0 12px;padding-left:20px}.old li{margin:0 0 8px}\n.tip{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px;font-size:18px}\n@media (max-width:420px){h1{font-size:24px}}\n</style></head><body><main>\n<p class=\"mut\">For Laura \u00b7 from Oleg</p>\n<h1>Why you got 29 posts on 14 October</h1>\n<p>This summer we rebuilt how posts are made from your interviews. The new way gives you one strong post per topic, checked against what you said. It just takes about an hour now.</p>\n<p>I never told you that. So when nothing showed up, you pressed \"Generate Content\", which runs the <b>old</b> way on top. That's where the extra posts came from. My mistake, sorry.</p>\n\n<h2>The difference</h2>\n<div class=\"box new\"><span class=\"badge\">New way \u00b7 5 posts, 5 different topics</span><div class=\"post\"><p>My daughter&#x27;s school has data proving no one can predict what jobs exist in 15 years, but you&#x27;re still hiring for today&#x27;s titles.</p><p>I visited my daughter&#x27;s school recently. She&#x27;s in first grade.</p><p>The employee walking me through it didn&#x27;t mention math levels or exam scores once.</p><p>What she said instead: they have data, based on huge market research, that we can&#x27;t even imagine what kind of positions are gonna be open in the future.</p><p>So the first years are built around how to adapt in new situations, how to be brave, how to talk properly, how to communicate, how to collaborate in different environments with different people.</p><p>Nobody can name the job titles coming. Not the school. Not us. Not the companies hiring right now.</p><p>I&#x27;m also seeing it in the kids. They compare themselves on soft skills now, not grades.</p><p>10-15 years ago none of us thought AI would answer a simple question, or that we&#x27;d have agents replacing assistants.</p><p>Math still matters. Hard subjects still sharpen the brain. But the school building the next generation stopped measuring kids by exam scores a while ago.</p><p>Makes me wonder what you&#x27;re still measuring candidates by.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"height:14px\"></div>\n<div class=\"box old\"><span class=\"badge\">Old button \u00b7 24 posts</span><p>14 of them retell the same intern story, for example:</p><ul><li>An intern scored the lowest possible result on an IQ test I gave her.</li><li>An intern took an IQ test. Lowest possible score.</li><li>A candidate scored the lowest possible result on the IQ test we use for hiring.</li></ul><p class=\"mut\" style=\"margin:0\">To fill 14 posts from one story it starts inventing things you never said, like \"founders visibly squirm\".</p></div>\n\n<h2>Next time</h2>\n<div class=\"tip\">After an interview, just wait about an hour. Your posts will appear on their own. No need to press anything.</div>\n</main></body></html>";
